# ◈ packages.browser.list — WebKitGTK + surf (replaces firefox)
#
# RENAMED from packages.firefox.list. Firefox was dropped after
# llvm-core/llvm-21.1.8 itself failed to compile — a genuine libc++
# template static-assertion bug (std::__map_value_compare / std::less<void>
# mismatch in LLVM's Hexagon backend), not a packaging mistake. Confirmed
# reproducible across two separate runs with identical output, so this
# isn't transient CI flakiness — it's LLVM 21.1.8 failing against this
# system's libc++ specifically.
#
# HONEST CAVEAT: WebKitGTK is also a large C++ codebase — comparable in
# scale to Firefox's own engine, if smaller. It may hit its own musl-
# specific build issues; this isn't a guaranteed smoother path, just a
# different, less enormous one worth trying. If it also fails, the
# build-report-browser.json from this group's release upload will have
# the real reason, same as it did for firefox and elogind.
#
# surf is the suckless project's minimal WebKit/GTK browser — pairs with
# the sway/dwm/st minimalism already established elsewhere in this repo.
#
# CORRECTED via a real run: net-libs/webkit-gtk's REQUIRED_USE needs
# any-of (aqua wayland X) and none were active by default. Enabled
# wayland specifically, matching this project's Wayland-first design
# already established in packages.graphics.list, rather than X (which
# would pull in the Xorg stack this project isn't defaulting to) or aqua
# (macOS-only, not relevant here).

net-libs/webkit-gtk           use:wayland
www-client/surf
